Two projects:

1) Scrape quotes.toscrape.com
  * Run scrapy runspider quotes_spider_w_mysql.py
  * Go to https://quotes.toscrape.com/tag/humor/ URL
  * Retrieve the items author and quote text from the page
  * Store the item objects to the QuotesProjectItem item class 
  * Follow the next page using the href tag
  * Retrieve the items author and quote text from the new page
  * Store the item objects to the QuotesProjectItem item class in items.py
  * Open the pipelines.py from the ITEM_PIPELINES in the settings.py 
  * Open an instance of a cursor and a mySQL database connection
  * Create the quotes table if iit does not exist
  * Save the author and text objects to the table
  * Close the database and cursor

2) Scrape the rosters from the Pittsburgh Steelers Super Bowl teams by year
* Run scrapy runspider Steelers_Super_Bowls.py -o steeler_super_bowl_rosters.csv to create csv file
* Go to https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pittsburgh_Steelers URL
* Retrieve the attributes of the Super Bowl championship years using XPath 
* From the attributes above retrieve the season year URLs using XPath
  - pass the year value in the .follow using a meta variable
* Follow the URLs
* Find the player roster list using XPath
* Retrieve the player name and roster year
* Store the item objects in the WikispiderItem class in items.py
* output the WikispiderItem class to a csv file "steeler_super_bowl_rosters"